.Ss Hooks
If defined,
.Nm
will run specially named user commands
.Po
.Dq hooks
.Pc
at certain predefined points during its execution.
Hook command names begin with
.Qq __
and end with
.Qq _hook .
Hooks take no formal parameters.
.Bl -tag -width __m2_file_suspend_hook -offset indent
.It Ic __m2_begin_hook
Invoked once at the beginning of
.Nm
execution, after any
initialization files are loaded.
.Va __FILE__
is undefined.
.It Ic __file_open_hook
Invoked whenever a new file is opened, but before its contents are read.
.Va __FILE__
is the newly opened file.
.It Ic __file_close_hook
Invoked whenever an included file has been read and closed.
.Va __FILE__
is still the recently closed file.
.It Ic __file_suspend_hook
Invoked whenever a new file is about to be included, temporarily
superseding the current input file..
.Va __FILE__
is the current, about to be suspended file.
.It Ic __file_resume_hook
Invoked whenever a previously suspended file is about to be resumed.
.Va __FILE__
is the newly resumed, originally current file.
.It Ic __m2_end_hook
Invoked after all input has been processed
but before any streams or wraps are executed.
.Va __FILE__
is undefined.
.It Ic __m2_exit_hook
Invoked at the very end of
.Nm
execution, just before exiting.
.El
.Ss Including Files
.Nm
can incorporate the contents of files into its data stream.
.Ic @include
retrieves and processes the file data for macros, while
.Ic @paste
reads the file contents with no modifications.
Attempting to
.Ic @include
or
.Ic @paste
a non-existent file results in an error.
However, if the
.Dq silent
variants
.Po
.Ic @sinclude ,
.Ic @spaste
.Pc
are used, no message is printed.
If
.Ic @include
or
.Ic @paste
cannot find the specified
.Va FILE
in the current directory,
it will consult the include path found in
.Va __INCPATH__ .
Directories can be inserted into the include path by specifying
.Ql I=<directory>
on the command line.
Paths specified this way are examined before entries from
.Ev M2PATH ,
to allow run-specific overrides.
The include path is also used, if needed, for file names passed on the
command line.
Elements may be removed from the include path by specifying
.Ql R=<directory>
on the command line.
.Ss Lists and Arrays
Arrays are stored internally as an Awk associative array, and can be
indexed by any literal value.  Lists are implemented with a different
mechanism that only allows integer indices.
.Pp
Arrays must be declared before use
by executing the command
.Ic @array
and specifying the name of the array to create.
After array declaration, its elements can be accessed
by using the array name immediately followed by the
element key in brackets; as always, surrounded by
.Ql @ .
.Pp
Lists must be declared before use
by executing the command
.Ic @list
and specifying the name of the list to create.
Lists are loaded with data by the
.Ic @data
or
.Ic @filedata
commands.
.Ic @data
requires the data to be present in\-line
in the input file, which is read until
.Ic @enddata .
If you wish to read your data from an external
file, use
.Ic @filedata .
Data loaded in this way are assigned integer
keys from 1 to the number records.
Lists can also be loaded with
.Ic @split .
.Pp
For both arrays and lists,
accessing the bare name, without brackets,
as in
.Ql @ Ns Ar ARRAY Ns @
will return the number of elements in the array or list.
.Ss Mathematical Expressions
The
.Ic @expr No ... Ns Ic @
function evaluates mathematical expressions and
inserts their results.
.Ic @expr@
supports the standard arithmetic operators:
.Dl (\ \ )\ \ +\ \ \-\ \ *\ \ /\ \ %\ \ ^
and the comparison operators:
.Dl <\ \ <=\ \ ==\ \ !=\ \ >=\ \ >
and return 0 or 1 as per Awk.
Logical negation is available with
.Ql \&! .
No other boolean operators are valid.
.Ql &&
and
.Ql ||
are
.Sy not supported !
.Po
However, see section
.Sx Boolean Expressions .
.Pc
.Pp
.Ic @expr@
supports the following functions:
.Pp
